Re-authored 2026-09-30 against v0.99.1. Upstream added image and
classifier models beside chat (#9948) and split recomposeProvider() into
compose + set so virtual models can wrap the result. Three changes:

1. The allowlist wrapper now filters getAllModels() as well as
   getModels(). withRemoteCatalog() adds a getAllModels() that returns
   chat models too, and it is what getModelsOfType(), getAllModels() and
   getAllAvailable() read; re-anchoring the v0.87 wrapper unchanged would
   have spread an unfiltered copy through and reopened every model of
   every type under deny-all. One set of `provider/model-id` globs covers
   all three types. Provider visibility counts models of every type.

2. The re-wrap of anything under a built-in id moved from
   setComposedProvider() into recomposeProvider(), before
   withVirtualModels(), so virtual entries stay listed.

3. New: prepareRequest() refuses a model under a built-in provider id
   that the allowlist denies. Every chat, deferred, image and classifier
   request passes through it, and the model there is the caller's object,
   not a catalogue lookup -- a constructed one, one restored from an old
   session, or the physical model a virtual model routes to would
   otherwise be dispatched. The filtered catalogue still decides what is
   offered; this decides what is sent.

Tests: deny-all empty across every type and read path, getAllModels()
filtered like getModels(), an image and a classifier model allowed only
when named, and dispatch refused for denied chat, image and classifier
models.

